
# Arduino Libraries

This directory contains the shared Arduino libraries used by packages in this
repository.

| Library | Description | Include |
|---|---|---|
| **NoPorts** | NoPorts daemon (sshnpd) — secure tunneling via atProtocol | `#include <NoPorts.h>` |

> **Note:** The `at_client` library (atSDK for ESP32) has moved to its own
> repository: [github.com/atsign-foundation/at_client_arduino](https://github.com/atsign-foundation/at_client_arduino).
> NoPorts depends on it — see below for installation instructions.

## Usage

### Arduino IDE

1. Install `at_client` first — download from [at_client_arduino releases](https://github.com/atsign-foundation/at_client_arduino/releases)
   or search for **at_client** in the Arduino Library Manager.
2. Copy the NoPorts library to your Arduino libraries directory:

       cp -r lib/NoPorts ~/Documents/Arduino/libraries/

### PlatformIO

Add both libraries to your project's `platformio.ini`:

    [env:esp32dev]
    platform = espressif32
    board = esp32dev
    framework = arduino
    lib_extra_dirs = ../../lib
    lib_deps =
      atsign-foundation/at_client
      NoPorts

See `packages/NoPorts/` for a complete reference project.
